[G8 PILOT] correction to the note above (checker 2026-10-25): 1,447 rows per coin in one day meant duplicated (coin, minute) labels, not extra minutes. The pilot extractor stored the first snapshot of every minute per hour file, and a minute at an hour boundary appears in two files (a snapshot stamped just before the hour sits in the next hour's file). No minute lies outside the day (0 rows before or after on 2025-07-15 and 2026-03-01). Duplicate rows: 2,824 on 2025-07-15, 4,414 on 2026-03-01. Stage fix in build8_l2.py (for the full run): sort by exchange time, keep the minimum per (coin, minute), assert uniqueness, drop and count rows outside the day, print both counts per day. Dry run on the stored 2025-07-15 table: 1,412 duplicates removed (2,824 rows = 1,412 pairs), maximum 1,440 rows per coin. The pilot parquet files were produced before this fix and are not used downstream.
